# Testing policy (garmin-collector)

## When tests are expected

- Code that **transforms, classifies, or shapes** data or errors: auth error types (429, 401), `failure_kind`, token load/dump, retry/backoff semantics, payload normalization before upload
- Changes to **`garminconnect/`** client behaviour that affect login, headers, or API error handling
- Bug fixes in those areas should include or extend a test where practical

Add or extend tests under **`tests/test_*.py`** excluding **`tests/test_garmin.py`** (upstream VCR; see below).

## When tests are NOT required

- README or env.example documentation only
- Log message wording with no behaviour change
- Operational notes in MAINTAINERS with no code change

## How to test

- Run **`pdm run test`** from repo root (see **`python-agent-verify.mdc`**) — **collector unit tests only**
- **`tests/test_garmin.py`** is upstream VCR baggage; not canonical verify. Use **`pdm run test-vcr`** only when explicitly syncing **`garminconnect/`** with upstream (do not re-record against live Garmin without user approval)
- Use **tdd-working-cycle** / **bdd-example-workshop** skills only when the user explicitly asks—not by default

## On failure

- Report expected vs actual before changing code
- For regressions, review local diff before altering established code
- Do not change a test to pass without explicit user approval
